  ("2.3" 0.1924 0.2270 0.1413 0.1566 0.1566 0.0153 nil 0.2896 0.0346 "KMLPCN+CMBX12" 0.0170 t nil 0)
  ("Function application" 0.2544 0.4971 0.1413 0.1566 0.1566 0.0153 0.00893 0.2411 0.1038 "KMLPCN+CMBX12" 0.0170 t nil 1)
  ("In mathematics, the application of a function to its arguments is usually de-" 0.1924 0.8120 0.1731 0.1848 0.1848 0.0117 0.00668 0.2767 0.0168 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 12)
  ("noted by enclosing the arguments in parentheses, while the multiplication of" 0.1924 0.8118 0.1892 0.2009 0.2009 0.0117 0.00686 0.2589 0.0447 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 10)
  ("two values is often denoted silently, by writing the two values next to one" 0.1924 0.8119 0.2053 0.2170 0.2170 0.0117 0.00837 0.2193 0.0283 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 13)
  ("another. For example, in mathematics the expression" 0.1924 0.6199 0.2214 0.2331 0.2331 0.0117 0.0064 0.2860 0.0662 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 6)
  ("f(a, b) + c d" 0.4552 0.5490 0.2500 0.2617 0.2617 0.0117 0.00409 0.4704 0.0329 "KMLPLK+CMMI10" 0.0130 nil t 4)
  ("means apply the function f to two arguments a and b, and add the result" 0.1924 0.8119 0.2788 0.2905 0.2905 0.0117 0.00812 0.2151 0.0500 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 14)
  ("to the product of c and d." 0.1924 0.4161 0.2949 0.3066 0.3066 0.0117 0.00878 0.1407 0.0162 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 6)
  ("Reflecting its primary status in the language," 0.4322 0.8115 0.2949 0.3066 0.3066 0.0117 0.0089 0.2828 0.0795 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 6)
  ("function application in Haskell is denoted silently using spacing, while the" 0.1924 0.8120 0.3110 0.3227 0.3227 0.0117 0.00868 0.2526 0.0657 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 10)
  ("multiplication of two values is denoted explicitly using the operator ∗. For" 0.1924 0.8115 0.3258 0.3388 0.3388 0.0117 0.00791 0.2506 0.1111 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 11)
  ("example, the expression above would be written in Haskell as follows:" 0.1924 0.7505 0.3431 0.3548 0.3548 0.0117 0.00615 0.2866 0.0707 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 10)
  ("f a b + c ∗d" 0.4477 0.5462 0.3727 0.3857 0.3857 0.0117 0.00528 0.3853 0.0056 "KMLPFO+CMTI10" 0.0130 nil t 5)
  ("Moreover, function application has higher priority than all other operators." 0.1924 0.8119 0.4005 0.4122 0.4122 0.0117 0.00794 0.2343 0.0791 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 9)
  ("For example, f a + b means (f a) + b. The following table gives a few fur-" 0.1924 0.8121 0.4166 0.4283 0.4283 0.0117 0.00738 0.3073 0.0266 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 17)
  ("ther examples to illustrate the differences between the notation for function" 0.1924 0.8116 0.4327 0.4444 0.4444 0.0117 0.00738 0.2278 0.0326 "KMLOPE+CMR10" 0.0130 nil nil 10)
